{% comment %}
  Popup: Email signup — native Wisepops replacement, built to the Claude
  Design handoff (Turn 4, options 4a–4f): bottom-left corner panel at the
  site gutter, no scrim, sign-up state swaps in place to a thank-you state
  (with or without discount code) inside an identical footprint.

  Each version block can optionally insert a phone-capture state between
  sign-up and thank-you (same pattern as the waitlist modal): skippable,
  input pre-seeded with the IP-detected country's calling code (market
  fallback), number normalised to international format and posted to
  Brevo's SMS attribute plus an identify and a popup_phone event
  (popup_phone_skip on skip). Requires the Brevo form URL — the phone
  state is not rendered on the Shopify customer-form fallback. Closing
  the popup during the phone state does NOT count as a dismissal: the
  email was already captured.

  Architecture (per interview):
  - Rendered site-wide from layout/theme.liquid as a static section; all
    campaign management happens in the theme editor (blocks = versions).
  - Signups create/update a Shopify customer via the customer form with
    marketing consent; tags carry campaign / variant / market path /
    language / discount code, and the existing Brevo–Shopify integration
    syncs them to Brevo. Language rides along on every signup, but no
    longer targets which version shows — markets do that.
  - Analytics: popup_impression / popup_submit / popup_dismiss events are
    pushed to window.dataLayer (or gtag) with campaign, experiment,
    variant, market, language and path_prefix — GA4's BigQuery export can
    then feed the BI dashboard. If neither exists the calls no-op.
  - A/B tests: give two (or more) versions the same Experiment name; each
    visitor is assigned a stable variant, split evenly.
  - Translations: recommend Shopify Translate & Adapt (theme content) —
    the block text fields are translatable there per language.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign skip_templates = 'cart,password,gift_card'
  assign tpl = template.name | append: ''
  assign skip = false
  if section.settings.hide_on_cart and skip_templates contains tpl
    assign skip = true
  endif
  if section.settings.enabled == false
    assign skip = true
  endif

  assign lang_code = localization.language.iso_code | downcase
  assign path_prefix = routes.root_url

  # Market key derived from the subfolder ('/en-au' -> 'au'); the root
  # domain is 'primary'. PATH is '' (not '/') on the primary market so
  # Brevo templates can build URLs as domain + PATH + /page for every
  # contact.
  assign market_key = 'primary'
  if path_prefix != '/'
    assign market_key = path_prefix | remove_first: '/' | split: '-' | last | downcase
  else
    assign path_prefix = ''
  endif

  # Warehouse serving this market, resolved exactly as stock-state does:
  # the metaobject whose domains list contains the market token ('main'
  # for the root domain), else the default-flagged one. Block targeting
  # matches typed codes against this warehouse's HANDLE — exact, or as
  # a prefix up to a hyphen ('au' matches 'au-3-pl-consumer'). With no
  # warehouse entries configured the popup falls back gracefully: codes
  # never match, so "All markets" mode still shows everywhere.
  assign wh_mk = 'main'
  if routes.root_url != '/'
    assign wh_mk = routes.root_url | remove_first: '/' | split: '-' | last | downcase
  endif
  assign popup_wh = ''
  assign popup_wh_default = ''
  for wh in settings.warehouses
    assign wh_h = wh.system.handle | downcase
    if wh.is_default.value and popup_wh_default == ''
      assign popup_wh_default = wh_h
    endif
    if wh.domains.value
      for wh_d in wh.domains.value
        assign wh_dd = wh_d | strip | downcase
        if wh_dd == wh_mk
          assign popup_wh = wh_h
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endfor
  if popup_wh == ''
    assign popup_wh = popup_wh_default
  endif
-%}

{%- unless skip -%}
{% style %}
  st-popup { display: contents; }
  .stp {
    position: fixed;
    left: 20px;
    bottom: 20px;
    width: 400px;
    max-width: calc(100vw - 40px);
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #e2e2e2;
    padding: 36px 36px 28px;
    z-index: 40;
    display: none;
  }
  /* Entry per the design handoff: fade ~280ms ease-out; mobile adds a
     10px rise (the sanctioned maximum — no full slides). Dismiss fades
     out ~180ms. The sign-up to thank-you swap stays instant
     (fixed-footprint rule). */
  @keyframes stp-fade-in {
    from { opacity: 0; }
    to { opacity: 1; }
  }
  @keyframes stp-rise-in {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
  @keyframes stp-fade-out {
    from { opacity: 1; }
    to { opacity: 0; }
  }
  .stp.is-open {
    display: block;
    animation: stp-fade-in 0.28s ease-out both;
  }
  .stp.is-open.is-closing { animation: stp-fade-out 0.18s ease both; }
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .stp.is-open { animation-name: stp-rise-in; }
    .stp.is-open.is-closing { animation-name: stp-fade-out; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .stp.is-open, .stp.is-open.is-closing { animation: none; }
  }
  /* Fixed footprint: both states share this box so nothing ever jumps */
  .stp__content { height: 345px; overflow: hidden; }

  .stp__close {
    position: absolute;
    top: 24px;
    right: 21px;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #121212;
  }

  .stp__eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 21px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: #121212;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .stp__heading {
    font-family: "Neue Haas Grotesk Display", var(--font-heading-family), sans-serif;
    font-size: 32px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: #000;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .stp__body {
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 21px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.6);
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }

  .stp__input {
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border: 1px solid #e2e2e2;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: #fff;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: #121212;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .stp__input::placeholder { color: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.55); }
  /* The black border is the focus state; suppress Dawn's offset outline,
     which the fixed-height panel clips into stray lines above and below */
  .stp__input:focus,
  .stp__input:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    box-shadow: none;
    border-color: #121212;
  }

  /* Matches the product page's add-to-cart button: sentence case,
     body-size Neue Haas Grotesk with no tracking, black fill */
  .stp__button {
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background: #161616;
    color: #fff;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    padding: 16px;
    cursor: pointer;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .stp__dismiss {
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 19px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.6);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.3em;
    cursor: pointer;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .stp__code-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    border: 1px solid #e2e2e2;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .stp__code {
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 21px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: #121212;
  }
  .stp__copy {
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 21px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: #121212;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.3em;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .stp__shop {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 21px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: #121212;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.3em;
  }
  .stp__state--thanks { display: none; }
  .stp__state--phone { display: none; }
  .stp.is-phone .stp__state--signup { display: none; }
  .stp.is-phone .stp__state--phone { display: block; }
  .stp.is-thanks .stp__state--signup,
  .stp.is-thanks .stp__state--phone { display: none; }
  .stp.is-thanks .stp__state--thanks { display: block; }

  /* Phone state: tightened spacing so the extra row (skip link) and
     consent line share the same fixed footprint as the other states —
     sized to the defaults (no eyebrow, two-line consent) on the 300px
     mobile box */
  .stp__state--phone .stp__body { margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .stp__state--phone .stp__button { margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .stp__smallprint {
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 18px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.55);
    margin: 8px 0 0;
  }
  .stp__error {
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 19px;
    color: #c8352e;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    display: none;
  }
  .stp.has-error .stp__error { display: block; }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .stp {
      left: 12px;
      right: 12px;
      bottom: 12px;
      width: auto;
      max-width: none;
      padding: 28px 24px 22px;
    }
    .stp__content { height: 300px; }
    .stp__close { top: 16px; right: 9px; }
    .stp__eyebrow { margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .stp__heading { font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .stp__body { margin-bottom: 20px; }
    .stp__button { min-height: 48px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<st-popup
  data-mode="{{ section.settings.trigger_mode }}"
  data-delay="{{ section.settings.delay_seconds | default: 6 }}"
  data-scroll="{{ section.settings.scroll_percent | default: 50 }}"
  data-dismiss-days="{{ section.settings.dismiss_days | default: 14 }}"
  data-signup-days="{{ section.settings.signup_days | default: 180 }}"
  data-session-cap="{{ section.settings.once_per_session }}"
  data-consent="{{ section.settings.respect_consent }}"
  data-design-mode="{% if request.design_mode %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
  data-market="{{ market_key }}"
  data-brevo-url="{{ section.settings.brevo_form_url }}"
  data-language="{{ lang_code }}"
  data-path-prefix="{{ path_prefix }}"
>
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign show_block = block.settings.enabled

      # Warehouse targeting: does any typed code match the warehouse
      # serving this visitor's market? Codes match the metaobject handle
      # exactly or as a hyphen prefix. "All markets, except…" hides on a
      # hit; "No markets, only…" shows only on a hit (so an empty list
      # there shows nowhere).
      if show_block
        assign wh_hit = false
        assign wh_codes = block.settings.wh_codes | downcase
        if wh_codes != blank and popup_wh != ''
          assign wh_code_list = wh_codes | split: ','
          for c in wh_code_list
            assign c_t = c | strip
            if c_t == blank
              continue
            endif
            if c_t == popup_wh
              assign wh_hit = true
              break
            endif
            assign c_dash = c_t | append: '-'
            assign wh_head = popup_wh | slice: 0, c_dash.size
            if wh_head == c_dash
              assign wh_hit = true
              break
            endif
          endfor
        endif
        if block.settings.visibility == 'none'
          assign show_block = wh_hit
        elsif wh_hit
          assign show_block = false
        endif
      endif

    -%}
    {%- if show_block -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign campaign = block.settings.name | default: 'popup' | handleize
        assign tags = 'newsletter,popup,campaign:' | append: campaign
        if block.settings.experiment != blank
          assign tags = tags | append: ',experiment:' | append: block.settings.experiment | handleize | append: ',variant:' | append: block.settings.variant | default: 'a' | handleize
        endif
        assign path_tag = path_prefix | default: '/'
        assign tags = tags | append: ',path:' | append: path_tag | append: ',lang:' | append: lang_code
        if block.settings.code != blank
          assign tags = tags | append: ',code:' | append: block.settings.code
        endif
        assign return_url = request.path | append: '?stp=thanks&stc=' | append: campaign
      -%}
      <aside
        class="stp"
        role="dialog"
        aria-modal="false"
        aria-label="{{ block.settings.heading | escape }}"
        data-stp-panel
        data-campaign="{{ campaign }}"
        data-experiment="{{ block.settings.experiment | handleize }}"
        data-variant="{{ block.settings.variant | default: 'a' | handleize }}"
        data-code="{{ block.settings.code | escape }}"
        {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
      >
        <button type="button" class="stp__close" data-stp-close aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M1 1l12 12M13 1L1 13" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/></svg>
        </button>

        <div class="stp__content">
          <div class="stp__state stp__state--signup">
            {%- if block.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
              <p class="stp__eyebrow">{{ block.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <h2 class="stp__heading">{{ block.settings.heading | escape }}</h2>
            {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
              <p class="stp__body">{{ block.settings.body | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if section.settings.brevo_form_url != blank -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Direct-to-Brevo form. Deliberately NOT Shopify's customer
                form tag: nothing in this form can reach /contact, so the
                captcha challenge can never force a page reload. onsubmit
                guard means even an unbound handler cannot navigate anywhere.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <form class="stp__form" data-stp-brevo action="{{ section.settings.brevo_form_url }}" method="post" onsubmit="return false">
                <p class="stp__error" data-stp-error>{{ section.settings.error_text | default: 'Something went wrong — please try again.' | escape }}</p>
                <input
                  type="email"
                  name="EMAIL"
                  class="stp__input"
                  placeholder="{{ block.settings.placeholder | default: 'Email address' | escape }}"
                  autocomplete="email"
                  required
                >
                <button type="submit" class="stp__button">{{ block.settings.button_label | default: 'Notify me' | escape }}</button>
              </form>
            {%- else -%}
              {%- form 'customer' -%}
                <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="{{ tags | escape }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="return_to" value="{{ return_url }}">
                <p class="stp__error" data-stp-error>{{ section.settings.error_text | default: 'Something went wrong — please try again.' | escape }}</p>
                <input
                  type="email"
                  name="contact[email]"
                  class="stp__input"
                  placeholder="{{ block.settings.placeholder | default: 'Email address' | escape }}"
                  autocomplete="email"
                  required
                >
                <button type="submit" class="stp__button">{{ block.settings.button_label | default: 'Notify me' | escape }}</button>
              {%- endform -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            <button type="button" class="stp__dismiss" data-stp-close>{{ block.settings.dismiss_label | default: 'No thanks' | escape }}</button>
          </div>

          {%- if block.settings.phone_enabled and section.settings.brevo_form_url != blank -%}
            <div class="stp__state stp__state--phone">
              {%- if block.settings.ph_eyebrow != blank -%}
                <p class="stp__eyebrow">{{ block.settings.ph_eyebrow | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              <h2 class="stp__heading">{{ block.settings.ph_heading | default: 'Be first in line' | escape }}</h2>
              {%- if block.settings.ph_body != blank -%}
                <p class="stp__body">{{ block.settings.ph_body | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}

              <form class="stp__form" data-stp-phone-form action="{{ section.settings.brevo_form_url }}" method="post" onsubmit="return false">
                <p class="stp__error" data-stp-phone-error
                  data-invalid-text="{{ block.settings.ph_error_text | default: 'Please enter your number including the country code.' | escape }}"
                  data-network-text="{{ section.settings.error_text | default: 'Something went wrong — please try again.' | escape }}"
                >{{ block.settings.ph_error_text | default: 'Please enter your number including the country code.' | escape }}</p>
                <input
                  type="tel"
                  name="SMS"
                  class="stp__input"
                  placeholder="{{ block.settings.ph_placeholder | default: 'Phone number' | escape }}"
                  autocomplete="tel"
                  data-stp-phone-input
                >
                <button type="submit" class="stp__button">{{ block.settings.ph_button_label | default: "Text me when they're on sale" | escape }}</button>
              </form>

              <button type="button" class="stp__dismiss" data-stp-phone-skip>{{ block.settings.ph_skip_label | default: 'No thanks, email is fine' | escape }}</button>

              {%- if block.settings.ph_smallprint != blank -%}
                <p class="stp__smallprint">{{ block.settings.ph_smallprint | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="stp__state stp__state--thanks">
            {%- if block.settings.ty_eyebrow != blank -%}
              <p class="stp__eyebrow">{{ block.settings.ty_eyebrow | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <h2 class="stp__heading">{{ block.settings.ty_heading | default: "You're on the list" | escape }}</h2>
            {%- if block.settings.ty_body != blank -%}
              <p class="stp__body">{{ block.settings.ty_body | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if block.settings.code != blank -%}
              <div class="stp__code-row">
                <span class="stp__code">{{ block.settings.code | escape }}</span>
                <button type="button" class="stp__copy" data-stp-copy data-copied-label="{{ block.settings.copied_label | default: 'Copied' | escape }}">{{ block.settings.copy_label | default: 'Copy' | escape }}</button>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            <a href="{{ block.settings.shop_url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="stp__shop">{{ block.settings.shop_label | default: 'Shop the store' | escape }} &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
</st-popup>

<script>
  class StPopup extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      this.panels = Array.from(this.querySelectorAll('[data-stp-panel]'));
      if (!this.panels.length) return;
      this.designMode = this.dataset.designMode === 'true';

      const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);

      // Tester's backdoor: ?stp=preview opens the popup immediately,
      // ignoring frequency caps and sending no analytics.
      if (params.get('stp') === 'preview') this.designMode = true;

      // Returning from a full-page (captcha-challenge) submit?
      if (params.get('stp') === 'thanks') {
        const panel = this.panels.find((p) => p.dataset.campaign === params.get('stc')) || this.panels[0];
        this.markSignedUp();
        this.openPanel(panel, true);
        return;
      }

      if (!this.designMode) {
        if (this.suppressed()) return;
        if (this.dataset.sessionCap === 'true' && this.session('stp:shown')) return;
      }

      this.panel = this.pickPanel();
      if (!this.panel) return;

      if (this.designMode) {
        if (this.dataset.designMode === 'true') {
          // Theme editor: stay hidden until the merchant selects the
          // section (or one of its version blocks) in the sidebar, and
          // hide again on deselect. Drives the class directly rather
          // than openPanel() so reopening works and no impression is
          // tracked while editing.
          document.addEventListener('shopify:section:select', (e) => {
            if (!e.target.contains(this) || !this.panel) return;
            this.bind(this.panel);
            this.panel.classList.add('is-open');
          });
          document.addEventListener('shopify:section:deselect', (e) => {
            if (!e.target.contains(this)) return;
            this.panels.forEach((p) => p.classList.remove('is-open'));
          });
          document.addEventListener('shopify:block:select', (e) => {
            this.panels.forEach((p) => {
              const hit = p === e.target || p.contains(e.target);
              p.classList.toggle('is-open', hit);
              if (hit) this.bind(p);
            });
          });
          return;
        }
        // ?stp=preview backdoor on the storefront: open immediately.
        this.openPanel(this.panel, false);
        return;
      }
      this.arm();
    }

    /* ---- storage helpers (all guarded: private mode etc.) ---- */
    store(k, v) { try { if (this.canPersist()) localStorage.setItem(k, v); } catch (e) {} }
    read(k) { try { return localStorage.getItem(k); } catch (e) { return null; } }
    session(k, v) {
      try {
        if (v !== undefined) { sessionStorage.setItem(k, v); return v; }
        return sessionStorage.getItem(k);
      } catch (e) { return null; }
    }
    canPersist() {
      if (this.dataset.consent !== 'true') return true;
      const cp = window.Shopify && window.Shopify.customerPrivacy;
      if (cp && typeof cp.userCanBeTracked === 'function') return cp.userCanBeTracked();
      return true;
    }

    daysAgo(ts) { return (Date.now() - Number(ts)) / 86400000; }

    suppressed() {
      const signed = this.read('stp:signed');
      if (signed && this.daysAgo(signed) < Number(this.dataset.signupDays)) return true;
      return false;
    }

    pickPanel() {
      const dismissDays = Number(this.dataset.dismissDays);
      const eligible = this.panels.filter((p) => {
        if (this.designMode) return true;
        const d = this.read('stp:dismissed:' + p.dataset.campaign);
        return !(d && this.daysAgo(d) < dismissDays);
      });
      if (!eligible.length) return null;

      const first = eligible[0];
      if (!first.dataset.experiment) return first;

      // Even, stable split between variants of the first eligible experiment
      const group = eligible.filter((p) => p.dataset.experiment === first.dataset.experiment);
      let r = this.read('stp:rand');
      if (r === null) { r = String(Math.random()); this.store('stp:rand', r); }
      return group[Math.floor(Number(r) * group.length) % group.length];
    }

    /* ---- triggers ---- */
    arm() {
      const mode = this.dataset.mode;
      const show = () => this.openPanel(this.panel, false);
      if (mode === 'immediate') {
        setTimeout(show, 2000);
      } else if (mode === 'exit') {
        if (window.matchMedia('(min-width: 750px)').matches) {
          this.onExit = (e) => { if (e.clientY <= 10) show(); };
          document.addEventListener('mouseout', this.onExit);
        } else {
          setTimeout(show, Number(this.dataset.delay) * 1000);
        }
      } else {
        this.timer = setTimeout(show, Number(this.dataset.delay) * 1000);
        this.onScroll = () => {
          const max = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
          if (max > 0 && window.scrollY / max >= Number(this.dataset.scroll) / 100) show();
        };
        window.addEventListener('scroll', this.onScroll, { passive: true });
      }
    }

    disarm() {
      clearTimeout(this.timer);
      if (this.onScroll) window.removeEventListener('scroll', this.onScroll);
      if (this.onExit) document.removeEventListener('mouseout', this.onExit);
    }

    /* ---- open / close / submit ---- */
    /* Shopify's own IP-derived country suggestion (first-party, powers its
       geolocation recommendations). Fetched once when the popup opens so
       submit is never delayed; empty string when unavailable. */
    fetchGeo() {
      if (this.geoFetched) return;
      this.geoFetched = true;
      this.geoCountry = '';
      fetch('/browsing_context_suggestions.json')
        .then((r) => r.json())
        .then((data) => {
          const d = (data && data.detected_values) || {};
          const c = d.country || {};
          this.geoCountry = d.country_name || c.name || c.handle || '';
          this.geoIso = (c.handle || '').toUpperCase();
        })
        .catch(() => {});
    }

    openPanel(panel, thanks) {
      if (this.opened) return;
      this.opened = true;
      this.disarm();
      this.fetchGeo();
      this.bind(panel);
      panel.classList.add('is-open');
      if (thanks) panel.classList.add('is-thanks');
      this.session('stp:shown', '1');
      if (!thanks) this.track(panel, 'popup_impression');
    }

    bind(panel) {
      if (panel.dataset.bound) return;
      panel.dataset.bound = '1';
      panel.querySelectorAll('[data-stp-close]').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          panel.classList.add('is-closing');
          setTimeout(() => panel.classList.remove('is-open', 'is-closing'), 180);
          // The phone state means the email was already captured — closing
          // there is not a dismissal of the campaign.
          if (!panel.classList.contains('is-thanks') && !panel.classList.contains('is-phone')) {
            this.store('stp:dismissed:' + panel.dataset.campaign, String(Date.now()));
            this.track(panel, 'popup_dismiss');
          }
        });
      });

      const phoneForm = panel.querySelector('[data-stp-phone-form]');
      if (phoneForm) {
        phoneForm.submit = function () {};
        phoneForm.addEventListener('submit', (e) => { e.preventDefault(); this.sendPhone(panel); });
        const skip = panel.querySelector('[data-stp-phone-skip]');
        if (skip) skip.addEventListener('click', () => {
          this.track(panel, 'popup_phone_skip');
          panel.classList.remove('is-phone', 'has-error');
          panel.classList.add('is-thanks');
        });
      }

      const form = panel.querySelector('form');
      // Third-party scripts (e.g. popup/marketing apps) have been observed
      // programmatically re-submitting newsletter forms, which bypasses
      // both submit listeners and onsubmit guards. The Brevo form never
      // native-submits, so neuter form.submit() outright.
      if (form && form.hasAttribute('data-stp-brevo')) form.submit = function () {};
      if (form) form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        panel.classList.remove('has-error');

        /* Preferred route: post straight to the Brevo form endpoint — this
           store's /contact endpoint always bounces background posts
           through the captcha challenge (full page reload), Brevo's
           doesn't. no-cors means the response is opaque; double opt-in
           on the Brevo form is the junk filter. */
        if (form.hasAttribute('data-stp-brevo')) {
          const emailInput = form.querySelector('input[type="email"]');
          const fd = new FormData();
          fd.append('EMAIL', emailInput ? emailInput.value : '');
          fd.append('email_address_check', '');
          fd.append('locale', 'en');
          // Attributes ride the form POST itself (atomic with the email —
          // immune to the tracker-vs-form contact-creation race). Brevo
          // maps them when matching fields exist on the form; extra
          // fields are ignored otherwise. The identify call remains as a
          // second channel.
          fd.append('POPUP_CAMPAIGN', panel.dataset.campaign);
          fd.append('POPUP_EXPERIMENT', panel.dataset.experiment || '');
          fd.append('POPUP_VARIANT', panel.dataset.experiment ? panel.dataset.variant : '');
          fd.append('MARKET', this.dataset.market || '');
          fd.append('LANGUAGE', this.dataset.language || '');
          fd.append('PATH', this.dataset.pathPrefix || '');
          fd.append('DISCOUNT_CODE', panel.dataset.code || '');
          if (this.geoCountry) fd.append('COUNTRY', this.geoCountry);
          fetch(form.action, { method: 'POST', body: fd, mode: 'no-cors' }).then(() => {
            this.markSignedUp();
            this.identify(form, panel);
            this.track(panel, 'popup_submit');
            if (panel.querySelector('[data-stp-phone-form]')) this.enterPhone(panel);
            else panel.classList.add('is-thanks');
          }).catch(() => panel.classList.add('has-error'));
          return;
        }

        fetch(form.action, {
          method: 'POST',
          body: new FormData(form),
          headers: { Accept: 'text/html' },
        }).then((resp) => {
          if (resp.url && resp.url.includes('/challenge')) {
            // Captcha required — let the browser do a real submit; the
            // return_to URL reopens the thank-you state after.
            form.submit();
            return;
          }
          this.markSignedUp();
          this.identify(form, panel);
          this.track(panel, 'popup_submit');
          panel.classList.add('is-thanks');
        }).catch(() => panel.classList.add('has-error'));
      });

      const copy = panel.querySelector('[data-stp-copy]');
      if (copy) copy.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const original = copy.textContent;
        const done = () => {
          copy.textContent = copy.dataset.copiedLabel;
          setTimeout(() => { copy.textContent = original; }, 2000);
        };
        if (navigator.clipboard) navigator.clipboard.writeText(panel.dataset.code).then(done, done);
        else done();
      });
    }

    markSignedUp() { this.store('stp:signed', String(Date.now())); }

    /* ---- phone state (same behaviour as the waitlist modal) ---- */

    enterPhone(panel) {
      panel.classList.remove('has-error');
      const input = panel.querySelector('[data-stp-phone-input]');
      // Seed the visitor's calling code — IP-detected country first,
      // market as fallback while geo is unresolved.
      if (input && !input.value) {
        const code = this.dialCode();
        if (code) input.value = '+' + code + ' ';
      }
      panel.classList.add('is-phone');
      if (input) input.focus();
      this.track(panel, 'popup_phone_impression');
    }

    dialCode() {
      if (!StPopup.DIAL) {
        StPopup.DIAL = {};
        ('AD376 AE971 AF93 AG1 AI1 AL355 AM374 AO244 AR54 AS1 AT43 AU61 AW297 AX358 AZ994 BA387 BB1 BD880 BE32 BF226 BG359 BH973 BI257 BJ229 BL590 BM1 BN673 BO591 BQ599 BR55 BS1 BT975 BW267 BY375 BZ501 CA1 CC61 CD243 CF236 CG242 CH41 CI225 CK682 CL56 CM237 CN86 CO57 CR506 CU53 CV238 CW599 CX61 CY357 CZ420 DE49 DJ253 DK45 DM1 DO1 DZ213 EC593 EE372 EG20 EH212 ER291 ES34 ET251 FI358 FJ679 FK500 FM691 FO298 FR33 GA241 GB44 GD1 GE995 GF594 GG44 GH233 GI350 GL299 GM220 GN224 GP590 GQ240 GR30 GT502 GU1 GW245 GY592 HK852 HN504 HR385 HT509 HU36 ID62 IE353 IL972 IM44 IN91 IO246 IQ964 IR98 IS354 IT39 JE44 JM1 JO962 JP81 KE254 KG996 KH855 KI686 KM269 KN1 KP850 KR82 KW965 KY1 KZ7 LA856 LB961 LC1 LI423 LK94 LR231 LS266 LT370 LU352 LV371 LY218 MA212 MC377 MD373 ME382 MF590 MG261 MH692 MK389 ML223 MM95 MN976 MO853 MP1 MQ596 MR222 MS1 MT356 MU230 MV960 MW265 MX52 MY60 MZ258 NA264 NC687 NE227 NF672 NG234 NI505 NL31 NO47 NP977 NR674 NU683 NZ64 OM968 PA507 PE51 PF689 PG675 PH63 PK92 PL48 PM508 PR1 PS970 PT351 PW680 PY595 QA974 RE262 RO40 RS381 RU7 RW250 SA966 SB677 SC248 SD249 SE46 SG65 SH290 SI386 SJ47 SK421 SL232 SM378 SN221 SO252 SR597 SS211 ST239 SV503 SX1 SY963 SZ268 TC1 TD235 TG228 TH66 TJ992 TK690 TL670 TM993 TN216 TO676 TR90 TT1 TV688 TW886 TZ255 UA380 UG256 US1 UY598 UZ998 VA39 VC1 VE58 VG1 VI1 VN84 VU678 WF681 WS685 XK383 YE967 YT262 ZA27 ZM260 ZW263')
          .split(' ').forEach((t) => { StPopup.DIAL[t.slice(0, 2)] = t.slice(2); });
      }
      let iso = this.geoIso || '';
      if (!iso) {
        const mk = this.dataset.market || '';
        iso = mk === 'primary' ? 'US' : mk === 'uk' ? 'GB' : mk.toUpperCase();
      }
      return StPopup.DIAL[iso] || '';
    }

    sendPhone(panel) {
      panel.classList.remove('has-error');
      const input = panel.querySelector('[data-stp-phone-input]');
      const errEl = panel.querySelector('[data-stp-phone-error]');
      let number = ((input && input.value) || '').replace(/[\s().\-]/g, '');
      if (number.slice(0, 2) === '00') number = '+' + number.slice(2);
      // Brevo's SMS attribute requires an international number
      if (!/^\+[1-9]\d{5,14}$/.test(number)) {
        if (errEl) errEl.textContent = errEl.dataset.invalidText;
        panel.classList.add('has-error');
        return;
      }
      const emailInput = panel.querySelector('input[type="email"]');
      const email = emailInput ? emailInput.value : '';
      // Same atomic form-POST pattern as the email step: the contact
      // already exists, so this is a pure attribute update on it.
      const fd = new FormData();
      fd.append('EMAIL', email);
      fd.append('email_address_check', '');
      fd.append('locale', 'en');
      fd.append('SMS', number);
      const phoneForm = panel.querySelector('[data-stp-phone-form]');
      fetch(phoneForm.action, { method: 'POST', body: fd, mode: 'no-cors' }).then(() => {
        try {
          if (window.Brevo && typeof window.Brevo.push === 'function') {
            window.Brevo.push(['identify', { identifiers: { email_id: email }, attributes: { SMS: number } }]);
            window.Brevo.push(['track', 'popup_phone', { email: email }, { data: { campaign: panel.dataset.campaign, market: this.dataset.market || '' } }]);
          } else if (window.sendinblue && typeof window.sendinblue.identify === 'function') {
            window.sendinblue.identify(email, { SMS: number });
            if (typeof window.sendinblue.track === 'function') window.sendinblue.track('popup_phone', { campaign: panel.dataset.campaign });
          }
        } catch (e) {}
        this.track(panel, 'popup_phone_submit');
        panel.classList.remove('is-phone');
        panel.classList.add('is-thanks');
      }).catch(() => {
        if (errEl) errEl.textContent = errEl.dataset.networkText;
        panel.classList.add('has-error');
      });
    }

    /* Write the signup context to Brevo contact attributes via Brevo's
       Marketing Automation tracker, when the site has it (their Shopify
       app installs it). Create matching attributes in Brevo first:
       POPUP_CAMPAIGN, POPUP_EXPERIMENT, POPUP_VARIANT, MARKET,
       LANGUAGE, PATH, DISCOUNT_CODE (all text). No-ops
       when the tracker is absent — the Shopify customer tags still
       carry the same data. */
    identify(form, panel) {
      const emailInput = form.querySelector('input[type="email"]');
      if (!emailInput || !emailInput.value) return;
      const attrs = {
        POPUP_CAMPAIGN: panel.dataset.campaign,
        POPUP_EXPERIMENT: panel.dataset.experiment || '',
        POPUP_VARIANT: panel.dataset.experiment ? panel.dataset.variant : '',
        MARKET: this.dataset.market || '',
        LANGUAGE: this.dataset.language || '',
        PATH: this.dataset.pathPrefix || '',
        DISCOUNT_CODE: panel.dataset.code || '',
      };
      // Only when detected — never blank a COUNTRY the order sync wrote
      if (this.geoCountry) attrs.COUNTRY = this.geoCountry;
      try {
        if (window.Brevo && typeof window.Brevo.push === 'function') {
          window.Brevo.push(['identify', { identifiers: { email_id: emailInput.value }, attributes: attrs }]);
        } else if (window.sendinblue && typeof window.sendinblue.identify === 'function') {
          window.sendinblue.identify(emailInput.value, attrs);
        }
      } catch (e) {}
    }

    /* popup_impression / popup_submit / popup_dismiss with campaign,
       experiment, variant, market, language, path_prefix — lands in
       dataLayer (GTM) or gtag (GA4 direct); no-ops without either. */
    track(panel, name) {
      if (this.designMode || !this.canPersist()) return;
      const payload = {
        campaign: panel.dataset.campaign,
        experiment: panel.dataset.experiment || null,
        variant: panel.dataset.experiment ? panel.dataset.variant : null,
        market: this.dataset.market || null,
        language: this.dataset.language,
        path_prefix: this.dataset.pathPrefix,
      };
      if (window.dataLayer) window.dataLayer.push(Object.assign({ event: name }, payload));
      else if (typeof window.gtag === 'function') window.gtag('event', name, payload);
    }
  }

  if (!customElements.get('st-popup')) customElements.define('st-popup', StPopup);
</script>
{%- endunless -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Popup: Email signup",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enabled", "label": "Enable popups", "default": true },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Trigger" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "trigger_mode",
      "label": "Show the popup",
      "options": [
        { "value": "delay_scroll", "label": "After a delay or scroll" },
        { "value": "exit", "label": "On exit intent (desktop)" },
        { "value": "immediate", "label": "Almost immediately" }
      ],
      "default": "delay_scroll"
    },
    { "type": "range", "id": "delay_seconds", "label": "Delay", "min": 0, "max": 30, "step": 1, "unit": "s", "default": 6 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "scroll_percent", "label": "…or after scrolling", "min": 10, "max": 90, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 50 },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Frequency" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "dismiss_days", "label": "Hide after dismissal", "min": 0, "max": 90, "step": 1, "unit": "d", "default": 14 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "signup_days", "label": "Hide after signup", "min": 0, "max": 360, "step": 5, "unit": "d", "default": 180 },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "once_per_session", "label": "At most once per session", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "hide_on_cart", "label": "Never show on the cart page", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "respect_consent", "label": "Respect cookie consent", "default": true, "info": "Waits for marketing consent (Shopify Customer Privacy) before storing frequency cookies or sending analytics events." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "error_text", "label": "Submission error message", "default": "Something went wrong — please try again." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Brevo" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "brevo_form_url", "label": "Brevo form URL", "info": "The action URL of a Brevo subscription form (…sibforms.com/serve/…). Signups then post directly to Brevo with no page reload. Leave empty to use Shopify's customer form instead (creates a Shopify customer, but this store's spam challenge makes the page briefly reload on submit)." },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Each block below is a popup version. Give two versions the same Experiment name to A/B test them (traffic splits evenly; events carry the variant). Analytics events popup_impression / _submit / _dismiss (and popup_phone_impression / _submit / _skip) go to GTM or GA4 when present. Signups become Shopify customers tagged with campaign, variant, market path and language — synced to Brevo. Translate popup text per language with Translate & Adapt." }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 8,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "version",
      "name": "Popup version",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Campaign name", "info": "Internal — used in tags and analytics. E.g. Out of stock 2026.", "default": "Out of stock" },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enabled", "label": "Enabled", "default": true },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Targeting" },
        { "type": "select", "id": "visibility", "label": "Markets", "options": [ { "value": "all", "label": "All markets, except…" }, { "value": "none", "label": "No markets, only…" } ], "default": "all" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "wh_codes", "label": "Warehouse codes", "info": "Comma-separated; matches the warehouse serving the visitor's market. Codes: us, au, eu, uk, hk, jp, kr, nz, sg, tw, go-bolt-yyz-5 (Canada). Empty list: All markets shows everywhere, No markets shows nowhere." },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Sign-up state" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "The Stendig" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Sold out for 2026" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body", "default": "Be the first to hear when next year's calendars go on sale." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "placeholder", "label": "Email placeholder", "default": "Email address" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Notify me" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "dismiss_label", "label": "Dismiss label", "default": "No thanks" },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Phone state" },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "phone_enabled", "label": "Ask for a phone number after signup", "default": false, "info": "Adds a skippable screen between sign-up and thank-you. The email is already recorded either way. Numbers post to Brevo's SMS attribute. Requires the Brevo form URL." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "ph_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "info": "Optional. The corner popup is small — on phones an eyebrow can push the smallprint out of view." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "ph_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Be first in line" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "ph_body", "label": "Body", "default": "Add your number and we'll text you the moment they go on sale" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "ph_placeholder", "label": "Phone placeholder", "default": "Phone number" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "ph_button_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Text me when they're on sale" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "ph_skip_label", "label": "Skip link label", "default": "No thanks, email is fine", "info": "Goes straight to the thank-you state." },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "ph_smallprint", "label": "Smallprint", "default": "By adding your number you agree to receive a text when calendars go on sale. Reply STOP to opt out." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "ph_error_text", "label": "Invalid number message", "default": "Please enter your number including the country code." },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Thank-you state" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "ty_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Thank you" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "ty_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "You're on the list" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "ty_body", "label": "Body", "default": "We'll email you when next year's calendars go on sale." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "code", "label": "Discount code", "info": "Optional. Shown in a copyable row and added to the signup's tags. Create the code itself in Discounts." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "copy_label", "label": "Copy label", "default": "Copy" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "copied_label", "label": "Copied label", "default": "Copied" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "shop_label", "label": "Shop link label", "default": "Shop the store", "info": "The arrow is added automatically." },
        { "type": "url", "id": "shop_url", "label": "Shop link", "info": "Defaults to the all-products collection." },
        { "type": "header", "content": "A/B test" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "experiment", "label": "Experiment name", "info": "Optional. Versions sharing a name are split evenly between visitors." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "variant", "label": "Variant label", "info": "E.g. A or B. Reported with every analytics event.", "default": "A" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
